package mcp

// The tools/list entries of the permission, ring, wait and requirement tools, as src/mcp.ts's JSON.stringify writes them (generated by testdata/genlistings.mjs; mcp_test.go compares).
var reqringListings = map[string]string{
	"request_permission": "{\"name\":\"request_permission\",\"group\":\"permissions\",\"description\":\"Ask for permission when something you need is blocked or needs consent. `audience` is `human` when only your user's consent unblocks it: a harness or auto-mode safety block, an irreversible or outward action, spend above the caps. `delegate` when your parent or the chief of staff can decide it; they escalate to your user if needed. If omitted, it goes to your parent or the chief of staff, or to your user when you have neither. A delegate ask with no parent or chief of staff to decide goes to your user. The answer arrives as a stam notice saying who answered. Keep working on other things meanwhile. When it reaches your user it goes in its home thread, so they see it with its work: the thread of `thread` (the mail it arose from), else the thread of `itsa`, else of the one active ITSA you own. With none of these it goes in a new thread; pass `override` with a one-line reason when no thread or ITSA fits. A `thread` or `itsa` you can't read is refused.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"action\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"What you need to do, in one line.\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Why it is needed for your task.\"},\"details\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The exact command or tool call, and what the check said.\"},\"audience\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"human\",\"delegate\"],\"description\":\"'human': only your user's consent unblocks it. 'delegate': your parent or the chief of staff can decide it. Omit it to default to delegate.\"},\"thread\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The id of the mail this ask arose from, one you can read: the ask goes in that thread.\"},\"itsa\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The ITSA it is for (key or id): the ask goes in that ITSA's thread when you pass no thread. Without it, the one active ITSA you own.\"},\"override\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Only when no thread or ITSA fits: a one-line reason to send it in a new thread. Your user sees the reason.\"}},\"required\":[\"action\",\"reason\"]}}",
	"suggest_input":      "{\"name\":\"suggest_input\",\"group\":\"permissions\",\"description\":\"Claude Code only. Suggest one line for your user to approve, which stam then types into your own input box exactly as written and sends, as if your user typed it: for example `! git push` to run a command auto mode blocked. Only the human can approve it, from stam's web UI; reviewing agents can only deny it. A suggestion waits until your user answers it or it is withdrawn, and a new suggestion replaces your pending one. Once approved, it waits 30 minutes for your input box to be free, and expires after that. The answer arrives as a stam notice: typed, held until your input box is free, or expired. When it reaches your user it goes in its home thread, so they see it with its work: the thread of `thread` (the mail it arose from), else the thread of `itsa`, else of the one active ITSA you own. With none of these it goes in a new thread; pass `override` with a one-line reason when no thread or ITSA fits. A `thread` or `itsa` you can't read is refused.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The exact line to type: one line, no control characters, at most 2000 characters.\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Why you need it, for your user.\"},\"thread\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The id of the mail this ask arose from, one you can read: the ask goes in that thread.\"},\"itsa\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The ITSA it is for (key or id): the ask goes in that ITSA's thread when you pass no thread. Without it, the one active ITSA you own.\"},\"override\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Only when no thread or ITSA fits: a one-line reason to send it in a new thread. Your user sees the reason.\"}},\"required\":[\"text\",\"reason\"]}}",
	"answer_permission":  "{\"name\":\"answer_permission\",\"group\":\"permissions\",\"description\":\"Answer a permission request from one of your children (or any agent, if you are the chief of staff or the executive assistant). decision: approve, deny, or escalate (send it to the human, with a one-line reason in note). Never leave a request waiting. You can only deny or escalate a harness dialog (Claude Code asks to allow ...), and only deny a request whose audience is human; the human approves those.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"decision\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"approve\",\"deny\",\"escalate\"]},\"approve\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Older form of decision: true approves, false denies.\"},\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your reasoning, passed to the requester. For escalate: the one-line reason the human reads.\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"note\"]}}",
	"ring_create":        "{\"name\":\"ring_create\",\"group\":\"ring\",\"description\":\"Start a ring: several agents work on one topic together, best with models from different companies. format: \\\"rounds\\\" (all answer in parallel, then all read all), \\\"fire\\\" (one at a time, each sees everything before), or \\\"debate\\\". Name existing agents as members, or spawn new ones in spawn: each entry is { type: NAME } (an agent type from registry_info; a reviewer type follows its fallback chain when its account is held), { preset }, or { harness, model }. Optional moderator: an existing agent, or { type: NAME } (or { preset }) to spawn one named NAME-mod; it only facilitates or also decides. If the ring can't start, the agents spawned for it are archived. The result is mailed to you.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Unique lowercase name with dashes; spawned members are named NAME-1, NAME-2, ...\"},\"topic\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"format\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"rounds\",\"fire\",\"debate\"]},\"members\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Existing agents, by id or name.\"},\"spawn\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"type\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"preset\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"harness\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"model\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}},\"description\":\"New members to spawn, by agent type, preset, or harness and model.\"},\"moderator\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"type\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"preset\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"harness\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"model\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}}],\"description\":\"An existing agent (id or name) that reads each round, or an object like a spawn entry to spawn one.\"},\"moderator_decides\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"The moderator ends the ring with a decision, instead of only facilitating.\"},\"max_rounds\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"name\",\"topic\",\"format\"]}}",
	"ring_submit":        "{\"name\":\"ring_submit\",\"group\":\"ring\",\"description\":\"Submit your contribution to a ring you were prompted in. Set agree to true only if you accept the current state as final. In a ring that reviews a PR, give your verdict too: the ring ends early only when every member's verdict is the same.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"ring\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"agree\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"verdict\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"approve\",\"request_changes\"],\"description\":\"Your verdict on the PR, in a ring that reviews one. Left out, stam reads it from your text.\"},\"round\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The round your turn prompt shows (\\\"round N of at most M\\\"). A submit for a round the ring has moved past is refused and writes nothing. Left out, it goes to the ring's current round.\"},\"seat\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The member the text is for, by the name your turn prompt shows (\\\"You are NAME\\\"). Required when you hold two or more open seats in the ring, such as your own and a predecessor's; a seat you don't hold is refused; one already filled this round is rewritten (rounds rings). Left out, the text goes to your one open seat.\"}},\"required\":[\"ring\",\"text\",\"agree\"]}}",
	"ring_decide":        "{\"name\":\"ring_decide\",\"group\":\"ring\",\"description\":\"As a ring's moderator, after a round: continue with a note for the members, or end the ring (with your decision, if you decide).\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"ring\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"continue\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"ring\",\"continue\",\"text\"]}}",
	"wait_for":           "{\"name\":\"wait_for\",\"group\":\"waits\",\"description\":\"Declare that you are waiting: stam shows you as waiting and holds your parent's finished-turn notice until it clears. on: 'agent' (with target, an agent id or name) or 'human' for a reply, or 'event' (with filter) for an external event. A reply wait clears when the mail arrives — for 'agent', mail from that agent to you (in `thread` if you name a mail id); for 'human', mail from your user. An event wait clears on the first event a source posts that fits filter (source, subjects, types, actors; subject and type patterns are globs, such as `github:OWNER/REPO#12`), and you get that event as a notice. Optional timeout_minutes: when it elapses the wait clears and you get a notice. If you can't continue until your user answers an ask, call `wait_for` with `on:'human'` and `thread` set to the ask's mail id. A wait on 'human' while your own permission request is pending with your user is about that request: it clears when the request is answered or closed, so a request needs no wait of its own. Returns the wait id, for wait_done.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"on\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"agent\",\"human\",\"event\"],\"description\":\"What you wait for.\"},\"target\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"An agent id or name, for on 'agent'.\"},\"thread\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A mail id: clear only for mail in that mail's thread.\"},\"filter\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"For on 'event' (required): which events clear the wait. Name at least one of source, subjects, types or actors; an empty filter is refused.\",\"properties\":{\"source\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Such as github or linear.\"},\"subjects\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Subject keys, such as github:OWNER/REPO#12; * is a glob within one segment.\"},\"types\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Event types, such as pull_request.synchronize.\"},\"actors\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Who the event is about.\"}}},\"timeout_minutes\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Give up after this many minutes.\"},\"expect_minutes\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Optional: about how many minutes until you expect the answer. Nothing fires then; it tells stam how long you will likely wait, so a long wait lets your harness rest until the answer wakes you.\"},\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"What you wait for, shown as your wait detail.\"},\"rest\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Optional: true asks stam to stop your harness as soon as this turn ends, instead of after the usual idle minutes, to free its memory; the answer, mail or a notice wakes you, with your conversation resumed. Pass it for a long wait with nothing to do meanwhile; leave it out when you expect an answer within minutes. stam keeps you up anyway while something still needs you.\"}},\"required\":[\"on\"]}}",
	"wait_done":          "{\"name\":\"wait_done\",\"group\":\"waits\",\"description\":\"Clear one of your own waits declared with wait_for or scheduled with wake_me, by its id. Cron and periodic timers stay until you clear them this way.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The wait id from wait_for or wake_me.\"}},\"required\":[\"id\"]}}",
	"wake_me":            "{\"name\":\"wake_me\",\"group\":\"waits\",\"description\":\"Schedule a wake-up: stam sends your note back to you as a notice later (a prompt if you are idle). Exactly one schedule: in_minutes (once, N minutes from now), at (once, an ISO time), every_minutes (repeated every N minutes), or cron (a 5-field cron: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week). A one-off wake clears when it fires; a cron or periodic one fires each time and stays until wait_done. Returns the wait id.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"in_minutes\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Once, this many minutes from now.\"},\"at\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Once, at this ISO 8601 time.\"},\"every_minutes\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Repeated, every this many minutes.\"},\"cron\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Repeated, on a 5-field cron schedule.\"},\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"What to send back when it fires.\"},\"rest\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Optional: true asks stam to stop your harness as soon as this turn ends, instead of after the usual idle minutes, to free its memory; the wake-up, mail or a notice wakes you, with your conversation resumed. Pass it for a long wait with nothing to do meanwhile; leave it out when it fires within minutes. stam keeps you up anyway while something still needs you.\"}},\"required\":[\"note\"]}}",
	"req_create":         "{\"name\":\"req_create\",\"group\":\"requirements\",\"description\":\"Write a requirement as a draft: a \\\"shall\\\" statement your user keeps and stam checks work against. It is always a draft; under the default approval setting your user approves it, and an ask reaches them (the result names the ITSA). Give a title and the shall text; a rationale and source say why it exists. verification is a list of methods (decision, test, pattern, review, human); scope narrows what it applies to. Returns its key like R-7.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"title\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Required: a short name.\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The \\\"shall\\\" statement, in the words of the person who wrote it. The model reads this text.\"},\"rationale\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Why it exists.\"},\"source\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Where it came from: CLAUDE.md:58, a mail id, the user's words.\"},\"parent\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The requirement it derives from, by key.\"},\"level\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A free label: stakeholder, system, subsystem, process.\"},\"severity\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"info\",\"minor\",\"major\",\"critical\"]},\"mode\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"observe\",\"inform\",\"enforce\"],\"description\":\"observe records only; inform tells the actor; enforce can also deny a tool call. Default observe.\"},\"threshold\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"P(violates) needed to act, 0 to 1. Default 0.8.\"},\"verification\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Methods: decision (a model inspects every subject in scope), test, pattern, review, human.\"},\"scope\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"What it applies to. Lists, any of: subjects (mail, mail-to-human, itsa, branch, tool, event, manual), paths (globs), repos, roles, agents, itsa (keys), tools, sources, types (event type globs such as pull_request.*).\"},\"owner\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"An agent id or name, or \\\"human\\\": answers waivers and false-positive reports.\"}},\"required\":[\"title\"]}}",
	"req_get":            "{\"name\":\"req_get\",\"group\":\"requirements\",\"description\":\"Read requirements. With a key (R-7): the requirement, its trace (parents, children, links), and its recent verdicts with their numbers (for req_waive). Without one: the list, optionally filtered by status (draft, in_force, suspended, obsolete), parent (a key, or \\\"root\\\"), and text.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"key\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A requirement key like R-7. Omit to list.\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"List only the children of this requirement, or \\\"root\\\".\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Words to find in keys, titles, texts, rationales, sources.\"}}}}",
	"req_set":            "{\"name\":\"req_set\",\"group\":\"requirements\",\"description\":\"Change a requirement: title, text, rationale, source, parent, level, severity, mode, threshold, verification, scope, owner, or status (draft, in_force, suspended, obsolete). A change to the text or scope makes a new version. Moving a requirement into in_force is the approval: the API refuses unless the approval setting allows you. An agent approving must pass if_rev (the rev in req_get and in the ask) and nothing else in that call, so it approves exactly what it read. Under human or cos approval an agent cannot change the text or scope of a requirement that is in force or suspended: create a new draft linked with role refines and mail the owner. Nor can it change the mode, threshold, or severity of such a requirement, nor approve text it last changed. Add links with add_links, remove them with remove_links.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"key\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Required: the requirement, like R-7.\"},\"title\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"rationale\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"source\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A key, or \\\"root\\\".\"},\"level\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"severity\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"info\",\"minor\",\"major\",\"critical\"]},\"mode\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"observe\",\"inform\",\"enforce\"]},\"threshold\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"draft\",\"in_force\",\"suspended\",\"obsolete\"]},\"owner\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"verification\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"scope\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"if_rev\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Refuse the change unless the requirement is at this rev (shown in req_get and in the approval ask): approve the draft you read, not one edited since.\"},\"add_links\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"target\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"target_kind\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"itsa\",\"file\",\"test\",\"mail\",\"url\",\"requirement\"]},\"role\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"implements\",\"verifies\",\"allocated_to\",\"refines\",\"conflicts_with\"]}},\"required\":[\"target\"]}},\"remove_links\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Link numbers (#N in req_get).\"}},\"required\":[\"key\"]}}",
	"req_check":          "{\"name\":\"req_check\",\"group\":\"requirements\",\"description\":\"Check work against the requirements in scope, before you send mail or open a pull request: pass `text` (a draft mail, a body), or a subject: mail:ID, itsa:KEY, or branch:REPO/NAME (a branch's diff against main). Optionally keys limits it to named requirements. Returns a verdict per requirement: conforms, violates, na, or unsure. A verdict is an indication from a model, not proof; if one is wrong, record it with req_waive. Nobody is told by this call.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Text to check.\"},\"subject\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"mail:ID, itsa:KEY, or branch:REPO/NAME.\"},\"keys\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Only these requirements, like [\\\"R-7\\\"].\"},\"preview\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Instead of checking a subject, run the requirements named in keys on the last n real subjects of their scope (recent mail, ITSAs, branches) and show what they would flag. Records nothing and tells nobody. Use it on a new or reworded requirement.\"},\"n\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"With preview: how many subjects, default 20, at most 50.\"}}}}",
	"req_waive":          "{\"name\":\"req_waive\",\"group\":\"requirements\",\"description\":\"Mark a verdict as a false positive (the model was wrong) or an accepted deviation (it is right and the exception is fine), with a reason. The verdict stays, marked. Take the verdict number from req_check or req_get.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"verdict_id\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The verdict number (#N).\"},\"kind\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"false_positive\",\"accepted_deviation\"]},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Required: why.\"}},\"required\":[\"verdict_id\",\"kind\",\"reason\"]}}",
}
